Run `alembic upgrade head` against a new database before starting the application.
The application no longer creates database tables automatically.

The initial migration creates users, roles, documents, and their relationships.
The latest migration adds persistent request audit events.

For an existing database created by the former `Base.metadata.create_all()` startup,
first verify that the users, roles, user_roles, documents, and document_shares tables
match revisions through `c13a6b0e8f42`. Then run:

    alembic stamp c13a6b0e8f42
    alembic upgrade head

Configure `DATABASE_URL` in the environment (or `.env`) before running Alembic.